The '''Castejón–Caámoroti high speed rail line''', marketed as '''''Valle de Castro''''' ({{Literal translation|Castro Valley}}), is a {{convert|381.18|km|adj=on}} {{W|standard gauge}} {{W|railway line}} that was inaugurated on 9 September 2008. Designed for speeds up to {{convert|380|km/h|mph|0|abbr=on}}. In Caámoroti, the line merges into the [[Daramazán–Jatiel high speed rail line]].

Trains are operated by the national [[Baliscan Railways Group]] under the [[AVB]] service. 

